{#-
  A document doc-class's table of contents (Stage 6c, design.md section 10.5).

  **One item, pointing at `index.md`.** A `toc.yml` is AEM's navigation, so every
  item in it promises the reader somewhere to land. A PDF is a download, not a
  page, and these folders have exactly one page -- the `index.md` beside this
  file, which already lists every artifact as a link. Listing the artifacts here
  too offered four destinations where there is one.

  `title` is the index's own title, so the nav entry and the page it opens agree.
  There is no `type` and no `bytes`: both described the artifact, and publishing
  `type: "md"` for a generated page invites something downstream to branch on it.

  The artifact list did not go away, it moved -- see `documents_index.md.j2`.
  Phase 9 rewrote this; `architecture.md` section 6.2.2 has the reasoning, and it
  is a deliberate reversal of the per-file rule that section used to carry.
-#}
